<title>CROATIA: Croatia January currency reserves fall to $4.1 bln.</title>
<headline>Croatia January currency reserves fall to $4.1 bln.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Croatia issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA CURRENCY RESERVES   JANUARY     DECEMBER    JAN '96</p>
<p> Total (million USD)	   4,086.9     4,306.1     3,241.0</p>
<p> National Bank of Croatia    2,173.1     2,314.0     1,845.2</p>
<p> Commercial banks		1,913.8     1,992.1     1,395.8</p>
<p>NOTE -- The central bank's January reserves shrank 6.1 percent from December 1996 and commercial banks' 3.9 percent. The National Bank of Croatia recently attributed the fall to a stronger dollar. -- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
